# nqt-vault (mandatory close-out)

Vault: `nqt-vault/` at repo root. Follow `.cursor/skills/nqt-vault/SKILL.md`.

**Do not mark a task complete, say "done", or stop a multi-step session until the vault is updated.** This is part of the work, not optional polish.

## Every completed task (feature, fix, install, research doc, rule)

1. Append a newest-first bullet to `nqt-vault/Project History/Change Log.md` with `[[wikilinks]]` to touched notes.
2. Update or create the matching note under Architecture / Components / Tabs / Guides (bidirectional links where useful).
3. Link new components from `nqt-vault/00 - Index.md` when you add a note.
4. Irreversible choice → new ADR in `Decision Log.md` (never edit an accepted ADR; supersede).
5. Optional session note: `Project History/YYYY-MM-DD - Title.md`.
6. **Commit completed work** with a conventional commit message once verified (stage only intended files; never stage `nqt-vault/.obsidian/workspace.json`, runtime data, or secrets; do not push unless asked).

## Do not

- Skip the vault because the change was "small" or "just a rule/install".
- Commit graphify HTML/JSON into the vault; keep artifacts gitignored.

If you cannot update the vault (permissions, etc.), say so explicitly before finishing — do not silently skip.
